// createSpawn
// partial score=0.9973 date=2026-09-28
// cl: /O2 /Ob2 /DNDEBUG /MD /EHsc /D_STLP_USE_STATIC_LIB
// ?createSpawn@SpawnBehavior@@AAE_NXZ
// 2026-09-28 opus-5.5: real extern globals, native bitset BitFlags<86>, team hoisted to a local, pinned callee spellings; 740/740 with 6 differing bytes (two temp-register choices).
// 2026-09-28 space-bunny-free: re-verified 740/740 with 6 differing bytes (EDX vs EAX at +0x97, EAX vs ECX at +0x1bf);
//   rotation_sweep 33 toggles + 30 source variants moved no byte; blocker=regalloc/scratch-temp-rotation.
// 2026-09-29 muse-spark-1.3-free: site 2 fixed (6->2 diffs) by reading parent producerID as a raw member load
//   (*reinterpret_cast<ObjectID*>((char*)parent + 0x78)) instead of the inline Object::getProducerID() getter:
//   the inline getter's EAX return-value habit produced mov eax,[ebp+0x78]/mov ecx,[GameLogic]/push eax,
//   while the raw load produces retail's mov ecx,[ebp+0x78]/push ecx/mov ecx,[GameLogic]. A non-const-cast
//   getter variant still gives EAX, so only the call-site raw load matches. Site 1 (+0x97 EDX vs EAX for the
//   m_spawnTemplate base feeding mov edi,[reg+0x4b4]) is immovable: cost/tmpl/nested-guard/!=0/split-decl/
//   holder-local/NULL-kill/orphan-guard/const-Player/non-const-holder/real-member-getter variants (shape_search
//   20+ trials) all keep EDX with identical bytes through +0x95; raw getCommandPoints folds to cmp-mem (worse).
//   Next: site 1 needs an upstream invisible-state change; try real Object/Player/ThingTemplate layouts from a
//   shared header (getProducerID/getCommandPoints as true member accesses) or retire as compiler-internal.
// 2026-09-29 space-bunny-free (2nd pass): site 1 is a C1 register-PREFERENCE residue, not a spelling error.
//   New evidence: (a) a standalone micro-lab (build/micro/{a..z1}.cpp + m.py/r.py, compile ~0.5 s) reproduces the
//   residue exactly -- a 60-line Spawn::f() with the same frame, the same reclaim/newSpawn block and the same
//   affordability chain compiles to `mov edx,[esi+0x34]; mov <callee-saved>,[edx+0x4b4]`, so the EDX is reachable
//   without the rest of the 740-byte body; (b) 40 further micro spellings all stay EDX: argument value 0/1/7,
//   static_cast and C-style casts on either side, `+0`, `(*p).commandPoints()`, `p->m_cp` data member instead of
//   the getter, const/non-const Holder and get, const/non-const `const ThingTemplate *m_spawnTemplate`,
//   `avail`/`cost` locals in both orders, both-locals, three-way `&&`, nested/else envelopes, `!(a >= b)`,
//   `a > b` reversed, `get(1) - cost < 0`, and making md/parent long-lived so EBP/EBX are occupied as in retail.
//   When the call result is a local the compiler stops hoisting (t3/u1: `cmp eax,[ecx+0x4b4]` with the load after
//   the call), which is why the local spellings cannot reach the retail form either; (c) a byte-level scan of
//   all 13 MB of retail .text shows the full `mov R1,[m]; mov R2,[R1+d32]; push imm8; call; cmp eax,R2; jcc`
//   shape occurs exactly ONCE in the whole image -- this body -- so there is no in-binary sample of the (eax,edi)
//   form to copy the spelling from, while a looser `mov R1,[m]; mov R2,[R1+d32]` scan does contain both
//   (eax,edi) x6 and (edx,edi) x2, i.e. the shape is reachable and this is a preference, not a codegen limit.
//   Verdict: site 1 is compiler-internal for this class of source; blocker=regalloc/c1-scratch-preference.
// 2026-09-29 muse-spark-1.3 (3rd pass): re-verified stash 740/740 with 2 non-reloc diffs (+0x97/+0x9a EDX vs EAX).
//   New hypothesis tested: controllingPlayer liveness forces EDX (double commandPoints() call keeps EAX live).
//   DISPROVED: single-call holder forms (nested-if holder local; assign-in-condition holder local) both compile
//   byte-identical to stash with the same EDX residue. Upstream bytes (through +0x95) and downstream bytes
//   (from +0xa7) are identical between retail and ours, so the temp choice is purely C1-internal for this DAG.
//   Verdict stands: blocker=regalloc/c1-scratch-preference.
// BFME SpawnBehavior::createSpawn reconstruction at retail RVA 0x0020C3B0.
// The local views preserve the BFME module and object offsets without shared-header edits.
